<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexander the Good</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1432</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Alexander I of Moldavia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexander the Good was prince of Moldavia from 1400 to 1432. His long, mostly peaceful reign consolidated the young principality: he organised its administration, obtained a metropolitan see recognised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, promoted trade through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suceava">Suceava</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bilhorod-dnistrovskyi">Cetatea Albă</a>, and allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, sending troops to Grunwald in 1410.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexander-the-good.jpg" alt="Alexander the Good" width="320" height="298" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ag0350835 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alexander_the_good.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
